      "title": [
       {
        "type": "heading6",
        "text": "What about content management?",
        "spans": []
       }
      ],
      "body_text": [
       {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "text": "The core concept of the design system is to offer users a comprehensive collection of versatile UI elements that can effectively present various types of content. It's important to note that content management systems (CMS) are not included in the design system's scope. Instead, individual channels are responsible for implementing their own CMS to manage and host content such as text and images. This separation allows the design system to focus on providing the necessary building blocks for consistent user interfaces while enabling full freedom of content management solutions at the channel level.",
        "spans": []
       }
      ],
      "caption": [],
      "cta_label": [],
      "cta_link": {
